# Sentinel

[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](LICENSE)

**Sentinel demonstrates production-inspired delivery semantics for security compliance agents, including at-least-once delivery, idempotent backend handling, durable retry queues, and crash recovery.**

This project reconstructs the core reliability patterns from distributed agent systems—content-addressable deduplication (SHA-256), explicit state machines, exponential backoff, and durable persistence—in a focused single-node implementation. It showcases engineering depth in delivery guarantees and fault tolerance without distributed infrastructure theater.

---

## Core Semantics

Sentinel implements reliability patterns from distributed agent systems:

- **At-Least-Once Delivery**: Durable retry queue with exponential backoff ensures reports reach backend
- **Crash-Safe Persistence**: Write-Ahead Logging (WAL) in SQLite prevents data loss on agent crashes
- **Content-Addressable Deduplication**: SHA-256 hashing enables idempotent backend processing
- **Explicit State Machine**: Formal delivery states (PENDING → RETRY → DELIVERED → FAILED)
- **Offline Operation**: Agent evaluates policies and queues reports when backend unavailable
- **Bounded Resources**: Hard limits on execution time (10s osquery, 1s Lua), memory, and output size

### System Architecture

